\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.3}{\ignorespaces The Strain Sensitivity of the aLIGO and A+ detectors. The noise due to radiation pressure and photon shot noise is shown in dark-blue (aLIGO) and dark-red (A+). Above 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, quantum effects are one of the limiting sources of noise; with the other being the noise due to Brownian motion of the mirror's coating. Below 10\tmspace  +\thinmuskip {.1667em}Hz, classical sources of noise, such as seismic motion, limit the sensitivity of both interferometers... figure out what is important to say here!\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.27}}
\newlabel{fig:detectorchapterdesignsensitivitycurves}{{1.3}{24}{The Strain Sensitivity of the aLIGO and A+ detectors. The noise due to radiation pressure and photon shot noise is shown in dark-blue (aLIGO) and dark-red (A+). Above 10\,Hz, quantum effects are one of the limiting sources of noise; with the other being the noise due to Brownian motion of the mirror's coating. Below 10\,Hz, classical sources of noise, such as seismic motion, limit the sensitivity of both interferometers... figure out what is important to say here!\relax }{figure.caption.27}{}}
